WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for opnmanager-walkthrough-1080p.mp4. The video is caption-led and has no
audio track; these cues mirror the on-screen text. Script: docs/walkthrough-script.md

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.700
OPNManager — self-hosted OPNsense fleet management for MSPs and IT teams

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.000
Every firewall you look after, grouped by customer and site.
All data shown is simulated demo data.

3
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.700
Start with what needs attention — roll-up tiles appear only when the count is non-zero

4
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.100
Eleven firewalls across five customers: one offline, four with updates pending,
two drifted from baseline

5
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.600
Workflow 1 — find the problem. One incident per ongoing condition, not one email per poll

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.400
Gateways, tunnels, services and certificates for a single firewall,
as reported by its agent

7
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.000
A degraded LTE gateway at 148 ms and 2.4% loss, and a stopped intrusion detection service

8
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.600
Workflow 2 — review what changed. Each firewall compared against the baseline you approved

9
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.600
Two firewall rules added since the baseline.
Serialisation noise is ignored, so an untouched firewall reports no drift

10
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.400
The whole interface has a light theme, with system preference detection and a manual toggle

11
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Workflow 3 — plan an update. Canary, then pilot, then production;
rings are a rollout mechanism, not customer tiers

12
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.200
HA pairs are never updated at the same time — the BACKUP member goes first

13
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.800
Maintenance windows scoped to a firewall, a site or a customer.
Collection continues; only notification is withheld

14
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Per-firewall traffic, load, memory and disk, collected on each agent check-in

15
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.600
Who did what, to which firewall, from where. Credential material is never recorded

16
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.800
Customers and sites are organisational groupings — they have no accounts and never log in

17
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.100
OPNManager — free and self-hosted. github.com/agit8or1/OPNMGR

18
00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:58.500
More free tools for MSPs — mspreboot.com
